{{Quote|Revan. Revan, Revan, Revan.|Cultists of the Sith Eternal speak Revan's name|<ref name="SotS">''[[Shadow of the Sith]]''</ref>}}
'''Revan''' was a [[Sith Lord]] and the namesake of the [[Sith Eternal]] [[Sith Eternal army|army's]] [[Revan Legion]]. Since the [[Timeline of galactic history|history]] of the [[Sith]] was kept hidden from [[the galaxy]], only [[Sith cultist]]s knew the significance of Revan's name.<ref name="TROS VD" /> In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="SotS date">The flashback in which Revan is mentioned in ''[[Shadow of the Sith]]'' takes place concurrently with [[Darth Vader (2020) 11|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 11]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of to [[3 ABY]].</ref> cultists searching the catacombs beneath the [[Sith Citadel]] on the [[planet]] [[Exegol]] repeated Revan's name in something similar to a chant, along with the names of other Sith.<ref name="SotS" />

[[Sith trooper]] [[legion]]s were each numerically identified and additionally named after an ancient Sith Lord. The Revan Legion was activated<ref name="TROS VD" /> in [[35 ABY]]<ref name="TROS date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of {{Film|IX}} to [[35 ABY]].</ref> along with the rest of the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]] during the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]].<ref name="TROS VD" />

